, "y1": 0.8087091757387247}, {"text": "132", "x0": 0.46813186813186813, "y0": 0.9572317262830482, "x1": 0.4912087912087912, "y1": 0.9665629860031104}], [{"text": "Question 7. (Use a separate hook.)", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.13919129082426127, "x1": 0.5076923076923077, "y1": 0.15085536547433903}, {"text": "(i) Find the values of m for which the equation", "x0": 0.17142857142857143, "y0": 0.1827371695178849, "x1": 0.6615384615384615, "y1": 0.19517884914463451}, {"text": "= me +9 = 0", "x0": 0.45604395604395603, "y0": 0.21228615863141523, "x1": 0.5703296703296703, "y1": 0.22161741835147744}, {"text": "has: (a) exactly one real root;", "x0": 0.2087912087912088, "y0": 0.24027993779160187, "x1": 0.5373626373626373, "y1": 0.2527216174183515}, {"text": "(b) real roots.", "x0": 0.2714285714285714, "y0": 0.2690513219284603, "x1": 0.42637362637362636, "y1": 0.2807153965785381}, {"text": "(ii) Michele buys five tickets in a raffle in which 20 tickets are", "x0": 0.16043956043956045, "y0": 0.3118195956454121, "x1": 0.8208791208791208, "y1": 0.32426127527216175}, {"text": "sold. Three different tickets are to be drawn out for first,", "x0": 0.2087912087912088, "y0": 0.3273716951788491, "x1": 0.8285714285714286, "y1": 0.33825816485225507}, {"text": "second and third prizes. Using a tree diagram find the", "x0": 0.2087912087912088, "y0": 0.34136858475894244, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.35303265940902023}, {"text": "probability that:", "x0": 0.2087912087912088, "y0": 0.3561430793157076, "x1": 0.3747252747252747, "y1": 0.36702954898911355}, {"text": "(a) Michele wins all three prizes;", "x0": 0.2703296703296703, "y0": 0.3849144634525661, "x1": 0.6175824175824176, "y1": 0.3965785381026439}, {"text": "(b) Michele does not win a prize;", "x0": 0.2703296703296703, "y0": 0.4129082426127527, "x1": 0.6065934065934065, "y1": 0.42534992223950235}, {"text": "(c) Michele wins at least one prize;", "x0": 0.2703296703296703, "y0": 0.44245723172628304, "x1": 0.6373626373626373, "y1": 0.45412130637636083}, {"text": "Michele wins exactly one prize.", "x0": 0.31758241758241756, "y0": 0.47200622083981336, "x1": 0.6263736263736264, "y1": 0.48289269051321926}, {"text": "133", "x0": 0.4824175824175824, "y0": 0.9541213063763608, "x1": 0.5043956043956044, "y1": 0.963452566096423}], [{"text": "Question 8. (Use a separate book.)", "x0": 0.13626373626373625, "y0": 0.13374805598755832, "x1": 0.4956043956043956, "y1": 0.14618973561430793}, {"text": "(i)", "x0": 0.15824175824175823, "y0": 0.1702954898911353, "x1": 0.1835164835164835, "y1": 0.18118195956454122}, {"text": "Figure not to scale", "x0": 0.6395604395604395, "y0": 0.29471228615863143, "x1": 0.8296703296703297, "y1": 0.3055987558320373}, {"text": "From a lighthouse L a ship $ bears 053\u00b0r and is at a", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.3856920684292379, "x1": 0.7692307692307693, "y1": 0.4020217729393468}, {"text": "distance of 8 nautical miles. From L a boat B bears 293\u00b0T", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.4051321928460342, "x1": 0.8296703296703297, "y1": 0.4144634525660964}, {"text": "and is at a distance of 6 nautical miles.", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.4191290824261275, "x1": 0.6054945054945055, "y1": 0.4284603421461897}, {"text": "(a) Draw a diagram marking on it the information supplied.", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.447900466562986, "x1": 0.7758241758241758, "y1": 0.4595645412130638}, {"text": "(b) Find the distance of ship $ from boat B. Give your", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.47667185069984447, "x1": 0.789010989010989, "y1": 0.48833592534992226}, {"text": "answer as a surd.", "x0": 0.23626373626373626, "y0": 0.49144634525660963, "x1": 0.4032967032967033, "y1": 0.5007776049766719}, {"text": "(c) Find the bearing of ship $ from boat B. Give your answer", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.5194401244167963, "x1": 0.8483516483516483, "y1": 0.531104199066874}, {"text": "to the nearest degree.", "x0": 0.23736263736263735, "y0": 0.5342146189735615, "x1": 0.45274725274725275, "y1": 0.5458786936236392}, {"text": "(ii)", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.5692068429237948, "x1": 0.1813186813186813, "y1": 0.5808709175738724}, {"text": "A particle moves in a straight line. At time t seconds its", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.5692068429237948, "x1": 0.8175824175824176, "y1": 0.5816485225505443}, {"text": "displacement x metres from a fixed point 0 on the line is", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.5839813374805599, "x1": 0.8065934065934066, "y1": 0.5956454121306376}, {"text": "given by", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.5987558320373251, "x1": 0.27362637362637365, "y1": 0.6104199066874028}, {"text": "x=3-cos2t, O< t< 2m", "x0": 0.3747252747252747, "y0": 0.6205287713841369, "x1": 0.6725274725274726, "y1": 0.6446345256609642}, {"text": "(a) Sketch the graph of x as a function of t.", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.6555209953343701, "x1": 0.6725274725274726, "y1": 0.6671850699844479}, {"text": "(b) Write down the times when the particle is at rest and the", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.6842923794712286, "x1": 0.8076923076923077, "y1": 0.6959564541213064}, {"text": "position of the particle at each of these times.", "x0": 0.23406593406593407, "y0": 0.6990668740279938, "x1": 0.7131868131868132, "y1": 0.7115085536547434}, {"text": "(c) Find the time when the particle first reaches its maximum", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.7278382581648523, "x1": 0.8076923076923077, "y1": 0.73950233281493}, {"text": "speed.", "x0": 0.23406593406593407, "y0": 0.7426127527216174, "x1": 0.29010989010989013, "y1": 0.7542768273716952}, {"text": "134", "x0": 0.4824175824175824, "y0": 0.9533437013996889, "x1": 0.5054945054945055, "y1": 0.9618973561430794}], [{"text": "Question 9. (Use a separate book.)", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.13374805598755832, "x1": 0.49340659340659343, "y1": 0.14541213063763608}, {"text": "(4) A person invests $800 at the beginning of each year in a", "x0": 0.15604395604395604, "y0": 0.1625194401244168, "x1": 0.7571428571428571, "y1": 0.1749611197511664}, {"text": "superannuation fund. Compound interest is paid at 10% per annum", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.17729393468118196, "x1": 0.8483516483516483, "y1": 0.18895800933125972}, {"text": "on the investment. The first $800 is to be invested at the,", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.19129082426127528, "x1": 0.8087912087912088, "y1": 0.20451010886469673}, {"text": "beginning of 1988 and the last is to be invested at the beginning", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.20606531881804044, "x1": 0.8472527472527472, "y1": 0.21850699844479005}, {"text": "of 2017. Calculate to the nearest dollar:", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.2208398133748056, "x1": 0.6230769230769231, "y1": 0.2301710730948678}, {"text": "(a) the amount to which the 1988 investment will have grown by", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.24883359253499224, "x1": 0.8175824175824176, "y1": 0.26127527216174184}, {"text": "the beginning of 2018;", "x0": 0.23516483516483516, "y0": 0.2643856920684292, "x1": 0.45274725274725275, "y1": 0.276049766718507}, {"text": "(b) the amount to which the total investment will have grown by", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.29237947122861585, "x1": 0.8263736263736263, "y1": 0.3048211508553655}, {"text": "the beginning of 2018.", "x0": 0.23516483516483516, "y0": 0.307153965785381, "x1": 0.45164835164835165, "y1": 0.3188180404354588}, {"text": "(ii) Tom took a bottle which had 200 millilitres of water in it. He", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.3359253499222395, "x1": 0.8373626373626374, "y1": 0.3468118195956454}, {"text": "poured more water into it for twenty seconds until it was full.", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.35069984447900465, "x1": 0.8241758241758241, "y1": 0.36236391912908245}, {"text": "During this time the volume flow rate R of water, in millilitres", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.3654743390357698, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.37636080870917576}, {"text": "per second, into the bottle was given by", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.37947122861586313, "x1": 0.5945054945054945, "y1": 0.3911353032659409}, {"text": "R= 4(20-t).", "x0": 0.42417582417582417, "y0": 0.40746500777604977, "x1": 0.5516483516483517, "y1": 0.4191290824261275}, {"text": "(a) Find a formula for the volume v of water in the bottle", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.43623639191290825, "x1": 0.7945054945054945, "y1": 0.447900466562986}, {"text": "after t seconds where t < 20.", "x0": 0.23186813186813188, "y0": 0.45023328149300157, "x1": 0.5406593406593406, "y1": 0.46111975116640747}, {"text": "(b) How many millilitres of water were in the bottle when it", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.4797822706065319, "x1": 0.7923076923076923, "y1": 0.49144634525660963}, {"text": "was full?", "x0": 0.23076923076923078, "y0": 0.49455676516329705, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.5038880248833593}, {"text": "(c) How long did it take before the bottle was half full?", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.5225505443234837, "x1": 0.7626373626373626, "y1": 0.5349922239502333}, {"text": "135", "x0": 0.4725274725274725, "y0": 0.947900466562986, "x1": 0.4945054945054945, "y1": 0.9564541213063764}], [{"text": "Question 10. (Use a separate book.)", "x0": 0.13626373626373625, "y0": 0.14541213063763608, "x1": 0.5054945054945055, "y1": 0.15707620528771385}, {"text": "(4) Find the number which when added to-each of 2, 6 and 13 will give", "x0": 0.15934065934065933, "y0": 0.18818040435458788, "x1": 0.8494505494505494, "y1": 0.19984447900466562}, {"text": "a set of three numbers in geometric progression.", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.20295489891135304, "x1": 0.6747252747252748, "y1": 0.21461897356143078}, {"text": "(di) A children's picture book is being designed so that each page", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.2317262830482115, "x1": 0.8087912087912088, "y1": 0.24339035769828926}, {"text": "contains 320 square centimetres of print and pictures surrounded", "x0": 0.1989010989010989, "y0": 0.24572317262830481, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.2581648522550544}, {"text": "completely by a white border as illustrated in the figure below.", "x0": 0.1989010989010989, "y0": 0.26049766718507, "x1": 0.8362637362637363, "y1": 0.2729393468118196}, {"text": "WHITE", "x0": 0.6054945054945055, "y0": 0.4097978227060653, "x1": 0.6527472527472528, "y1": 0.41601866251944014}, {"text": "BORDER", "x0": 0.6054945054945055, "y0": 0.4214618973561431, "x1": 0.654945054945055, "y1": 0.42923794712286156}, {"text": "\u00a9", "x0": 0.3021978021978022, "y0": 0.4354587869362364, "x1": 0.310989010989011, "y1": 0.4440124416796267}, {"text": "Figure not to scale", "x0": 0.5989010989010989, "y0": 0.4681181959564541, "x1": 0.7879120879120879, "y1": 0.4797822706065319}, {"text": "Each page is to have a border of width 2 centimetres at the bottom", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.604199066874028, "x1": 0.8593406593406593, "y1": 0.6174183514774495}, {"text": "and on each side, as well as a border of width 3 centimetres at", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.619751166407465, "x1": 0.8274725274725274, "y1": 0.6306376360808709}, {"text": "the top.", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.635303265940902, "x1": 0.27362637362637365, "y1": 0.6461897356143079}, {"text": "Let the width of a page be x centimetres and its length be y", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.6625194401244168, "x1": 0.8285714285714286, "y1": 0.6741835147744946}, {"text": "centimetres.", "x0": 0.1967032967032967, "y0": 0.6780715396578538, "x1": 0.3131868131868132, "y1": 0.687402799377916}, {"text": "(a) Show that the area A square centimetres of one such page is", "x0": 0.2, "y0": 0.7130637636080871, "x1": 0.8483516483516483, "y1": 0.7247278382581649}, {"text": "given by:", "x0": 0.23736263736263735, "y0": 0.7286158631415242, "x1": 0.321978021978022, "y1": 0.73950233281493}, {"text": "25].", "x0": 0.5692307692307692, "y0": 0.7457231726283048, "x1": 0.6043956043956044, "y1": 0.7744945567651633}, {"text": ". 320", "x0": 0.4472527472527473, "y0": 0.7488335925349923, "x1": 0.5714285714285714, "y1": 0.76049766718507}, {"text": "(b) Prove that the page which fulfils all the printing requirements", "x0": 0.1989010989010989, "y0": 0.7986003110419907, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.8110419906687403}, {"text": "given and which has the smallest area is 20 centimetres wide", "x0": 0.23736263736263735, "y0": 0.8133748055987559, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.8250388802488335}, {"text": "and 25 centimetres long.", "x0": 0.23626373626373626, "y0": 0.828149300155521, "x1": 0.4736263736263736, "y1": 0.8390357698289269}, {"text": "\u2018The Copyright of this examination paper is vested in Her Majesty, and reproduction in part or", "x0": 0.1901098901098901, "y0": 0.880248833592535, "x1": 0.7901098901098901, "y1": 0.8926905132192846}, {"text": "full, without the express permission of the Board of Senior School Studies, is not permitted.", "x0": 0.1901098901098901, "y0": 0.8911353032659409, "x1": 0.7901098901098901, "y1": 0.9020217729393468}, {"text": "136", "x0": 0.4703296703296703, "y0": 0.9471228615863142, "x1": 0.4945054945054945, "y1": 0.9564541213063764}]]